## Run

```bash
go run ./cmd/server
```

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `GRPC_ADDR` | `:{{.Port}}` | Listen address |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error` (JSON logs on stdout) |
{{- if .Postgres}}
| `DATABASE_URL` | unset | PostgreSQL connection URL; unset uses the in-memory store, which loses data on restart. Pool settings go in the URL, e.g. `?pool_max_conns=20` |
{{- end}}
| `TLS_CERT_FILE`, `TLS_KEY_FILE` | unset | Serve TLS 1.3; rotated files are picked up without a restart |
| `TLS_CLIENT_CA_FILE` | unset | Require client certificates signed by this CA (mTLS) |
| `REQUEST_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Deadline for calls that arrive without one; `0s` turns it off |
| `MAX_IN_FLIGHT` | `1024` | Concurrent calls before new ones get `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`; `0` turns it off |
| `MAX_CONNECTION_AGE` | `5m` | Recycle connections so load balancers can rebalance |
| `DRAIN_DELAY` | `0s` | Report NOT_SERVING this long before stopping (5s in the Kubernetes manifest) |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `10s` | Time allowed for in-flight calls on shutdown |
{{- if .OTel}}
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | unset | Enables OTLP traces and metrics when set |
{{- end}}

Health: the overall and `{{.FullServiceName}}` health services report
readiness{{if .Postgres}}, which follows the database{{end}}; the `liveness` service reports that
the process runs. Reflection is on, so grpcurl works:

```bash
grpcurl -plaintext localhost:{{.Port}} list
{{- range .Entities}}{{if .HasCreate}}
grpcurl -plaintext -d '{{.ExampleJSON}}' localhost:{{$.Port}} {{$.FullServiceName}}/Create{{.Name}}
{{- end}}{{end}}
```

## Develop

```bash
make generate        # regenerate Go code from the proto (buf)
make test            # go test -race -cover ./...
{{- if .Postgres}}
make test-postgres   # the store contract against PostgreSQL in Docker
{{- end}}
make lint            # buf lint, go vet, golangci-lint
make docker          # build the container image
```
{{- if .Examples}}

The acceptance examples from the spec live in
`internal/service/acceptance_test.go`. They fail until the custom methods are
implemented: they are the definition of done.
{{- end}}

## Deploy
{{if .Kubernetes}}
`kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s` creates a Deployment (gRPC probes, non-root,
read-only root file system), a Service and a PodDisruptionBudget.{{if .Postgres}} Put the
database URL in a secret named `{{.Name}}-db` with the key `url`.{{end}}
{{- end}}
{{if .CI}}
`.github/workflows/ci.yml` lints, checks breaking changes, runs the race tests{{if .Postgres}}
against PostgreSQL{{end}}, runs golangci-lint and govulncheck, and builds the image.{{end}}

## Layout

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `proto/` | API contract |
| `gen/` | Code generated by buf. Do not edit |
| `cmd/server` | Entry point: config, store, TLS, graceful shutdown |
| `internal/config` | Environment configuration |
| `internal/server` | gRPC server, interceptors, TLS, health, reflection |
| `internal/service` | Handlers, validation, acceptance and fuzz tests |
| `internal/store` | Repository interface, in-memory store{{if .Postgres}}, PostgreSQL store and migrations{{end}} |
{{- if .Kubernetes}}
| `deploy/k8s` | Kubernetes manifests |
{{- end}}
| `.fliessband/manifest.json` | Origin and hash of every generated file |
